# Difficulty 0 — a crime is never free
#
# open_door is difficulty 0, and an eager means would take it lower still — but standing in the Test
# Room, which is private, makes ANY act trespass, and an illegal act is floored at 1
# (Verb.ActionDifficulty): what a failed crime costs (the witness who hears it and comes) is the whole
# crime chain, and an act that cannot fail could never be heard. So the door out is rolled, at ①, and
# `strategy fail-dice` makes it miss. By night: the weaver is asleep in it, and awake she would confront
# whoever walked in before anything else could be looked at.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --willingness eager --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Room" --period night --observe-only "Test Room Door"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

expect-state where trespass=yes

strategy fail-dice
goal open_door
advance 12 180

click observe "Test Room Door"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Room Door"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180

expect-state trees difficulty=1
expect-no-state trees difficulty=0

click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb open_door
expect-no-outcome area_move
quit
